This connected planar drawing has a loop at $R$ and two edges joining $P$ and $Q$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (1.5,2.6);
\draw (P)--(Q);
\draw (P) .. controls (1.0,-0.9) and (2.0,-0.9) .. (Q);
\draw (Q)--(R);
\draw (R)--(P);
\draw (R) .. controls (0.3,4.2) and (2.7,4.2) .. (R);
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\node[left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[left] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use Euler's formula to find the number of faces.
